# Line endings that survive a clone on any system: text files normalised,
# the shell script always LF (a CRLF shebang does not run), the batch file
# always CRLF (cmd's `set /p` needs it), and binaries left alone.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.dbc -text
*.blp -text
*.m2 -text
*.skin -text
*.wav -text
*.ogg -text
*.mpq -text
